#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:349
msgid ""
"2025 was the first year all reports were submitted using Github. We report "
"on the issues the group received in 2025, or on issues that were received "
"earlier, but were disclosed in 2025."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:353
msgid "We group the issues into the following categories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:355
msgid "Security issues fixed under a coordinated disclosure process (2 issues)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:356
msgid ""
"Supply chain security related issues and project services-related issues (2 "
"issues)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:358
msgid ""
"Issues deemed to not require coordinated action before disclosing publicly "
"(11 issues)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:360
msgid "Invalid issues (5 issues)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:362
msgid ""
"In 2025, we received 2 invalid issues that we believe that have been created "
"automatically and 1 issue appeared to be created using generative AI. That "
"issue was considered to be invalid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:368
msgid ""
"This section lists the reported issues where we ended up implementing fixes "
"under a coordinated disclosure process. The security advisories for those "
"issues can be found at <https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/"
"advisories/>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:373
msgid ""
"“CMSE secure state may leak from stack to floating-point registers” {{ br }} "
"Details are available at [GHSA-wh65-j229-6wfp](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-"
"security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-wh65-j229-6wfp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:376
msgid ""
"“Binary executable injection vulnerability in clang-linker-wrapper."
"exe” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-hrx2-grgx-9vhg](https://github."
"com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-hrx2-grgx-9vhg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:382
msgid ""
"“Critical Supply Chain Vulnerability in RockstarGames/llvm-project "
"(CVE-2025-30066)” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-3fq9-qcq4-8jjr]"
"(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-3fq9-"
"qcq4-8jjr) {{ br }} The issue had already been fixed with commit "
"[6616acd80cd91](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/"
"commit/6616acd80cd91a0075e3cd481bb9a6d82fd4ea9e)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:388
msgid ""
"“CVE-2022-25883 and CVE-2022-3517 with respect to llvm-project/mlir/utils/"
"vscode/package-lock.json” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-g72r-487m-"
"m6hh](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-"
"g72r-487m-m6hh) {{ br }} Packages have been updated with [PR 144479](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/144479)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:397
msgid ""
"“Coroutine Frame-Oriented Programming: A new exploitation method using C++ "
"coroutines” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-v8pv-j8f5-qqcg](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-v8pv-j8f5-qqcg) "
"{{ br }} The researchers shared a new exploitation method that leverages the "
"implementation of C++ routines. Their [paper](https://www.usenix.org/"
"conference/usenixsecurity25/presentation/bajo) describing the technique has "
"been published and is available publicly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:404
msgid ""
"“Security Bug in String Assign Function (libc++)” {{ br }} Details are "
"available at [GHSA-m967-6j3p-jrwc](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-"
"repo/security/advisories/GHSA-m967-6j3p-jrwc) {{ br }} There has been an "
"agreement that the proof of concept had undefined behavior which makes it "
"out of scope according to [the LLVM threat model](https://llvm.org/docs/"
"Security.html#what-is-considered-a-security-issue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:410
msgid ""
"“[clangd] heap-use-after-free in clangd when generating "
"diagnostics” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-5426-9r4h-7whf](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-5426-9r4h-7whf) "
"{{ br }} It has been agreed this report fell out of scope because it was "
"caused by untrusted inputs, as described in [the LLVM threat model](https://"
"llvm.org/docs/Security.html#what-is-considered-a-security-issue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:416
msgid ""
"“A compiler optimization bug may cause signed integer overflow detection be "
"bypassed” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-w6jm-h8j9-q33r](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-w6jm-h8j9-q33r) "
"{{ br }} There has been an agreement that the PoC had undefined behavior "
"which makes it out of scope according to [the LLVM threat model](https://"
"llvm.org/docs/Security.html#what-is-considered-a-security-issue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:423
msgid ""
"“libomp: Crash (OOB Write / ASan BUS Error) involving omp_init_lock under "
"high concurrency” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-cfhc-jxq2-97mf]"
"(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-cfhc-"
"jxq2-97mf) {{ br }} The group agreed to close this as not a security issue "
"because the code was written without taking into consideration the "
"expectations from the OpenMP specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:430
msgid ""
"“[MLIR] head-use-after-free in mlir-lsp-server on completion "
"request” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-8j9r-qc4r-q9fh](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-8j9r-qc4r-q9fh) "
"{{ br }} This report fell out of scope because it was caused by untrusted "
"inputs, as described in [the LLVM threat model](https://llvm.org/docs/"
"Security.html#what-is-considered-a-security-issue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:436
msgid ""
"“[clangd/clang] heap-buffer-overflow in clang/lib/Sema/SemaExprCXX."
"cpp:9144” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-qq8q-r524-8vw9](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-qq8q-r524-8vw9) "
"{{ br }} This issue and the following 3 were concluded to be outside of the "
"[LLVM threat model](https://llvm.org/docs/Security.html#what-is-considered-a-"
"security-issue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:441
msgid ""
"“[clangd] heap-buffer-overflow in clang/lib/Sema/SemaExprCXX."
"cpp:8876” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-3xm9-vccr-fxx5](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-3xm9-vccr-fxx5)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:444
msgid ""
"“[clangd/clang] heap-use-after-free at clang/Sema/Ownership.h:81” {{ br }} "
"Details are available at [GHSA-qj36-2p7g-83gv](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-"
"security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-qj36-2p7g-83gv)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:447
msgid ""
"“Clang 20.1.0 Compiler Internal Error (Crash) during AST Parsing of C+"
"+23” {{ br }} Details are available at [GHSA-p2g2-89wf-7gcm](https://github."
"com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/advisories/GHSA-p2g2-89wf-7gcm)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SecurityTransparencyReports.md:450
msgid ""
"“Compiler-induced non-constant-time code” {{ br }} Details are available at "
"[GHSA-627p-g235-23pm](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-security-repo/security/"
"advisories/GHSA-627p-g235-23pm) {{ br }} The reporters shared a pre-print "
"article evaluating non-constant-time code generated by Clang. We all agreed "
"this did not need coordinated disclosure because Clang offers no guarantees "
"of constant-time code."
msgstr ""

